{"type": "spr", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"one seventh left parenthesis x minus k right parenthesis left parenthesis 16 minus x squared right parenthesis equals 0\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the given equation, <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> is a positive constant. The sum of the solutions to the equation is <math alttext=\"59\"><mn>59</mn>\n</math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math>?</p>", "keys": ["59"], "rationale": "<p>The correct answer is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"59\"><mn>59</mn></math>. It's given that in the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"one seventh left parenthesis x minus k right parenthesis left parenthesis 16 minus x squared right parenthesis equals 0\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> is a positive constant. Multiplying both sides of this equation by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn></math> yields&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus k right parenthesis left parenthesis 16 minus x squared right parenthesis equals 0\"><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. By the zero product property, it follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x minus k equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"16 minus x squared equals 0\"><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Adding&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> to both sides of the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x minus k equals 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> yields&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals k\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></math>. Adding&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x squared\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> to both sides of the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"16 minus x squared equals 0\"><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> yields&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"16 equals x squared\"><mn>16</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4 equals x\"><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 4 equals x\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>. Therefore, the solutions to the given equation are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn></math>, and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 4\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. It's given that the sum of the solutions to the equation is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"59\"><mn>59</mn></math>. Thus,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k plus 4 plus left parenthesis negative 4 right parenthesis equals 59\"><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>59</mn></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k equals 59\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>59</mn></math>.</p>", "externalid": "7f98a663-e37c-478d-90b1-a6bf6fc13f6b", "correct_answer": ["59"]}